This render-phase guard calls `deepEqual` on two `Set<string>` objects on every render. Deep-comparing Sets is a recursive, expensive operation — the codebase's own guidance (PERF-11) notes `deepEqual` on `Set`/`Map` is "extremely slow." Since this comparison runs each render just to decide whether to call `setUnconfirmedTransactionIDs`, it adds unnecessary overhead where a cheap shallow check suffices.

Replace the deep comparison with a shallow size + membership check (which is equivalent for a `Set<string>`):

```ts
const hasSameUnconfirmedIDs =
    nextUnconfirmedTransactionIDs.size === unconfirmedTransactionIDs.size &&
    [...nextUnconfirmedTransactionIDs].every((id) => unconfirmedTransactionIDs.has(id));

if (!hasSameUnconfirmedIDs) {
    setUnconfirmedTransactionIDs(nextUnconfirmedTransactionIDs);
}
```

`paginationSkeletonReasonAttributes` has the same issue — it is a plain object literal recreated on every render, causing unnecessary `useEffect` executions in `useSkeletonSpan`.

Wrap in `useMemo` to match the established codebase pattern:
```tsx
const paginationSkeletonReasonAttributes = useMemo<SkeletonSpanReasonAttributes>(
    () => ({
        context: 'AddUnreportedExpense.PaginationSkeleton',
        isLoadingUnreportedTransactions,
        hasMoreUnreportedTransactionsResults,
        isOffline,
    }),
    [isLoadingUnreportedTransactions, hasMoreUnreportedTransactionsResults, isOffline],
);
```

