`initialSkeletonReasonAttributes` is created as a plain object literal on every render without `useMemo`. This object is passed as `reasonAttributes` to `UnreportedExpensesSkeleton`, which forwards it to `useSkeletonSpan`. Inside `useSkeletonSpan`, a `useEffect` depends on `reasonAttributes`, so a new object reference on every render causes `span.setAttributes()` and `span.addEvent()` to fire unnecessarily.

Every other usage of `SkeletonSpanReasonAttributes` in this codebase wraps the object in `useMemo` (see `PlaidCardFeedIcon.tsx`, `AvatarCropModal.tsx`, `Lightbox/index.tsx`).

Wrap in `useMemo`:
```tsx
const initialSkeletonReasonAttributes = useMemo<SkeletonSpanReasonAttributes>(
    () => ({
        context: 'AddUnreportedExpense.InitialSkeleton',
        isLoadingUnreportedTransactions,
    }),
    [isLoadingUnreportedTransactions],
);
```

